{"id": "EUVD-2026-75022", "enisaUuid": "4adf9579-076d-3655-b05d-74bbd8062d73", "description": "zstd-jni before 1.5.7-14 fails to validate the samples buffer capacity in Zstd.trainFromBufferDirect, allowing attackers to read past buffer boundaries by supplying oversized per-sample lengths. Attackers can trigger out-of-bounds memory access by providing crafted sample length arrays that cause the native implementation to walk past the buffer allocation, resulting in JVM termination.", "datePublished": "2026-09-09T14:32:44", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-20T00:35:32", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/luben/zstd-jni/security/advisories/GHSA-257p-3h6w-pg7h", "https://github.com/luben/zstd-jni/commit/bba6cfca2c0897f1fa004f4193247479f10da853", "https://github.com/luben/zstd-jni/blob/v1.5.7-13/src/main/native/jni_zdict.c", "https://github.com/luben/zstd-jni/blob/v1.5.7-13/src/main/java/com/github/luben/zstd/Zstd.java", "https://github.com/luben/zstd-jni/releases/tag/v1.5.7-14", "https://github.com/luben/zstd-jni/commit/53d3c6342883f7d6717b2477a7f9c1b4a4a56980", "https://github.com/luben/zstd-jni", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/zstd-jni-1.3.3-1-through-1.5.7-13-out-of-bounds-read-via-zstd-trainfrombufferdirect"], "aliases": ["GHSA-v36p-vv44-8qfg", "CVE-2026-87824"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.39, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "c33224be-7cd4-37b2-b13d-37a9e9cf1ade", "product": {"name": "zstd-jni", "vendor": {"name": "luben"}}, "product_version": "1.3.3-1 <1.5.7-14"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "0a9c74ca-d526-3b77-86b8-a377d6d1b56a", "vendor": {"name": "luben"}}], "isExploited": false}